PRIMARY ACCEPTANCE SHAPE

The structural-trust-region thesis is supported if:

- E materially outperforms IMMEDIATE BLASTEMA on cost / action downtime in LOCAL-5 and LOCAL-10 without worse structural safety;
- E materially outperforms UNBOUNDED PATCH in DIFFUSE-20 and STACKED final topology quality;
- E recognizes that LOCAL-10 and DIFFUSE-10 require different responses despite equal magnitude;
- cumulative debt causes R5 handoff before repeated small patches recreate H143 scaffold anchoring;
- spatial diffusion improves R3/R4 handoff relative to CUMULATIVE-DEBT alone;
- R7 transient local noise rarely launches blastema;
- R8 high-value-local can increase repair urgency without automatically forcing global redevelopment;
- unaffected certificate inheritance saves substantial revalidation cost;
- false inherited-certificate rate remains <1% primary;
- blastema is not active continuously;
- recovery remains within bounded evidence cost.

FAILURE CONDITIONS

Treat H147 as mixed/negative if:

- trust-region thresholds simply reproduce immediate blastema;
- local patching provides no cost / downtime advantage;
- same-magnitude local vs diffuse damage produces indistinguishable behavior;
- cumulative micropatches evade handoff;
- certificate inheritance creates stale action;
- preserving certificates erases the safety benefit of redevelopment;
- blastema launches frequently on transient local noise;
- cumulative debt grows permanently under harmless repair;
- trust-region metrics require latent true damage labels;
- evidence / compute approaches always-on full reconstruction.

